## Configuration

The smokeforge generator writes `.env` from `.env.example`. Never commit
`.env`; it is gitignored and may contain secrets generated locally.

| Variable | Required | Used by | Notes |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL` | yes | Metadata, OpenGraph, sitemap, robots | Absolute app URL. Defaults to `http://localhost:3000` for local development. |
| `NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL` | no | API client | External API origin for standalone apps. Leave unset for same-origin `/api` routes. Must be an absolute URL. |
| `DATABASE_URL` | database overlay | Drizzle | Postgres connection string. Use `@localhost` for local dev and `@db` inside Docker Compose. |
| `BETTER_AUTH_SECRET` | auth overlay | Better Auth | Generate with `openssl rand -base64 32`. Never commit it. |
| `BETTER_AUTH_URL` | auth overlay | Better Auth | Absolute app origin used for auth callbacks. |
| `BETTER_AUTH_TRUSTED_ORIGINS` | no | Better Auth | Comma-separated additional origins if the app is served elsewhere. |
| `RESEND_API_KEY` | auth email | Better Auth email | Required for production OTP delivery. |
| `EMAIL_FROM` | auth email | Better Auth email | Verified sender for Resend. |
| `LOG_LEVEL` | no | Pino | `trace`, `debug`, `info`, `warn`, `error`, or `fatal`. |
| `NEXT_PUBLIC_POSTHOG_KEY` | analytics overlay | PostHog | Public project key. Analytics remains disabled when unset. |
| `NEXT_PUBLIC_POSTHOG_HOST` | no | PostHog | Defaults to US cloud; set an EU or self-hosted host if needed. |
| `PORT` | no | Node/Docker runtime | Docker sets `3000`; override only when required. |

Database, auth, and PostHog variables are documented but only used when their
overlays are selected. Analytics must not capture until the user opts in.

## API and errors

- `GET /api/health`
- `POST /api/v1/echo` is the validation/error example.
- Business routes belong under `/api/v1/**/route.ts`.
- Success: `{ "data": ... }`
- Error: `{ "error": { "code", "message", "fields"? } }`
- Throw `AppError` from `@/lib/api/app-error` and wrap handlers with
  `withApi` from `@/lib/api/handler`. The helper maps thrown errors to the
  single response shape and logs unexpected failures with Pino.
- Validate input with Zod (`parseJson`) and authorize inside every protected
  route handler.
- Keep secrets server-side; never expose them through `NEXT_PUBLIC_*`.

## Metadata and SEO

`src/app/layout.tsx` uses the Metadata API. `opengraph-image.tsx`, `sitemap.ts`,
and `robots.ts` provide social images and crawl rules. `robots.ts` blocks
`/api/` but keeps `/_next/`, CSS, JS, and images crawlable.

## Authentication

Selecting the auth overlay wires Better Auth sessions with email/password and
6-digit OTP flows:

- `/signup`, `/login`, `/verify-email`, `/forgot-password`, `/reset-password`
- `/dashboard` is server-protected
- `POST /api/auth/**` is the Better Auth Route Handler
- Local development prints OTPs to the server log. Production requires
  `RESEND_API_KEY` and `EMAIL_FROM`; non-local hosts fail closed without them.
- Start the local database with `make db-up`. It requires Docker and gives an
  installation hint if Docker is missing or not running.

## Logging

Server code uses `logger` from `@/server/logger` (Pino). Set `LOG_LEVEL` to
control verbosity. Do not log secrets or production OTPs.

